# Intended Dutch changes of the UI layer (vendor/ui), contracts C3; notes/claude/plan.md ground rule "Dutch stays
# default and byte-identical". Owner: GE1a and later UI steps. Checked by:
#   tests/i18n/run.sh --record --accept ID,…          (the UI text dump against tests/i18n/baseline-nl.txt)
#   python3 -B tools/i18n/check_ui.py --dict-diff tests/i18n/dict-nl-3b898e6.tsv
#                                                     (every makeT/{nl,en}/P()/X_NL text against Codex's 3b898e6)
# One line per change, tab-separated:
#   STEP<TAB>surface id,id,… or a file<TAB>why          a changed block of baseline-nl.txt (a new block needs no line),
#                                                     or a change of rendering code that no single key carries
#   STEP<TAB>key:<file below vendor/ui/js>:<key><TAB><the new nl text exactly, TSV escapes \n \t \\; - = removed><TAB>why
#       a dictionary row whose nl changed or disappeared (required), or a new key with a new Dutch text (optional)
# A key moved out of a Dutch-only literal into a dictionary with the same text needs no line (the dict diff lists it
# as added; the dump shows the same text): bridge.js, search.js qq_*/FALLBACK_SETTINGS, the Alles tip examples and
# q_todayQuery, Verkenner's shortcut/extFile/tab texts, picker saveAs, Alles firstNoteNative, startmenu clear,
# update exportName.
# Coordinator defaults (notes/claude/plan.md D-G1a, D-G1b, D-G2), offered to Robin in the final report: D-G1a
# accepted (singulars for 1, "1.000 items"), D-G1b held back (endonym, Afbeelding, Alles wording), D-G2 (GNOME-wrong
# texts rewritten in both languages).
